WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:06.490
Agent Carla Mendoza was one of the best field
agents that Site 41 had ever seen.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:11.270
She was professional, cool under pressure,
and when the situation demanded it, she could

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.330
be a straight-up badass.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:18.350
During a Chaos Insurgency raid on the Site,
she’d single handedly killed four different

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.240
insurgents - the last one with her bare hands.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.610
During containment breaches, she’d always
be the first one charging into the fray, her

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.740
Foundation standard-issue Beretta drawn and
ready to fire.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.060
Agent Mendoza was so devoted to the job that
she took up the Site Director’s offer to

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:41.239
start living onsite, so she could always be
there to help if an emergency situation unfolded.

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:46.520
After all, when it all hits the fan, you want
someone as utterly unshakeable as Agent Mendoza

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.980
on your side.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.610
The job had thrown the worst of the worst
at her, and she’d never even flinched.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.530
So surely, nothing could scare Agent Mendoza,
right?

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.550
Right?

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.900
After a long day of kicking ass, taking names,
and filling in the properly mandated amount

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:08.340
of SCP Foundation debriefing paperwork, Agent
Mendoza retired to her Site 41 quarters.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.409
She felt exhausted and sweaty, so before heading
to bed to watch some wonderful SCP Explained

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.959
videos on her phone, she decided to take a
quick shower.

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:25.009
The last thing she expected was for this particular
shower to become...well, let’s say “Hitchcockian.”

00:01:25.009 --> 00:01:29.479
The water was running, hot and clean, filling
the air with steam.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:34.799
Agent Mendoza was lathering up her hair when
she first heard the noise: Heavy, wheezing

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:38.659
breaths coming from just behind the shower
curtain.

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:43.670
The second she heard it, Agent Mendoza felt
a kind of brutal, crushing anxiety that she’d

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.770
never experienced before.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.429
Like a hand was reaching into her chest, and
squeezing her heart.

00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:54.689
The self-defense training that’d been encoded
into her muscle memory over years of working

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:56.999
at the Foundation kicked into effect.

00:01:56.999 --> 00:02:02.200
In a blind panic, she struck out at the shower
curtain, causing it to sway outwards - and

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.249
land directly on the face of Mendoza’s wheezing
voyeur.

00:02:06.249 --> 00:02:12.350
Who or whatever it was, it was standing right
there, less than a meter away from the shower.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:16.540
That wheezing carved into Mendoza’s ears
like a butcher’s knife.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:19.470
What an awful, monstrous sound.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:24.000
And despite the fact that the shower curtain
obscured its face, she could still somehow

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.340
see it, the way a defenseless animal can sense
an approaching predator without ever locking

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:35.050
eyes on it - and just somehow know that it’s
too late for them to escape now.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:40.090
Every training session, every achievement,
every piece of battle-hardening experience

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.480
- it all evaporated in the presence of that
thing.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.210
Mendoza was so terrified, she might as well
have been a child.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:53.790
The monster just stood there beyond the curtain,
its raw, fleshy face parted into a freakishly

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.870
wide, yellow-toothed grin.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.900
She didn’t know how, but on some deep, primal
level, she was aware that if this thing got

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.840
its hands on her, something horrific beyond
description would happen to her.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.070
She was too terrified to even move a muscle
in its presence.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:14.940
She remained like that, standing in the shower
and sobbing quietly, for the next three solid

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.910
hours until the creature finally disappeared.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.770
When her colleagues found her, she’d experienced
moderate scalding wounds from the hot water

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:23.950
of the shower.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:28.800
It took another several hours for Agent Mendoza
to compose herself enough to share her story.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.680
A couple of days later, Tim Ellis, a junior-level
filing clerk, was found trapped in a Site

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.970
41 supply closet.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:40.930
He’d urinated in his Foundation-issue slacks,
and was in a state of borderline catatonia.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:45.650
When his superiors asked him why he’d been
spending two hours in a supply closet on company

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.280
time, he reported that it was because a monster
had appeared outside the door when he was

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.100
searching for a replacement stapler.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:57.900
Despite never actually opening the door to
see what was outside or call for help - Mr.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.080
Ellis said that he felt as though he would
have had a heart attack if he actually opened

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.510
that accursed door - he was able to provide
a clear description of the monster.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:13.150
He said it was tall and emaciated, with reddish-brown
skin that made it seem almost burnt or rotten.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:18.129
While it stood there and waited beyond the
supply closet door, it let out the most awful

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:22.069
wheezing noise, like an old, rusty Iron Lung.

00:04:22.069 --> 00:04:29.250
But the image that Ellis seemed most fixated
on was the monster’s face, or lack thereof:

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:35.259
Just a huge, grinning mouth that covered up
its entire head, stocked with an arsenal of

00:04:35.259 --> 00:04:36.340
massive, yellow teeth.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.400
Ellis was visibly shivering as he talked about
it.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:45.860
Two incidents are an unpleasant coincidence,
but three are a bonafide pattern, and it didn’t

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:51.550
take long for more sightings of this strange
new anomaly - dubbed SCP-303, or The Doorman

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.219
- to pop up across the site.

00:04:54.219 --> 00:04:58.789
It earned that name by always appearing behind
some kind of doorway, or at least a movable

00:04:58.789 --> 00:05:02.710
divider, in the case of Agent Mendoza’s
shower curtain.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.400
Whenever it appeared outside a doorway, nearby
Foundation personnel would report being struck

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:12.940
with a sudden paralyzing terror that made
engaging with the creature impossible.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:16.960
Attempts to call for help were also often
stifled, as the very presence of the Doorman

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.069
causes disruptions to electrical equipment.

00:05:20.069 --> 00:05:24.699
Whenever The Doorman manifests in your proximity,
it’s safe to say that it’ll be commanding

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:27.849
your absolute, undivided attention.

00:05:27.849 --> 00:05:32.509
This was a particularly frightening case for
the SCP Foundation because it was one of the

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:36.490
few anomalies bringing the fight directly
to them.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:41.909
Most sentient anomalous beings would do anything
to avoid getting captured by the SCP Foundation

00:05:41.909 --> 00:05:46.740
and contained in one of their high-security
sites, full of experienced researchers and

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:51.180
state-of-the-art equipment designed specifically
to neutralize their effects.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:56.310
The Doorman, however, just seemed to take
this as a challenge, turning even the most

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:00.889
hardcore personnel on the site into gibbering
wrecks with its mere presence.

00:06:00.889 --> 00:06:05.009
But The Doorman was just getting started.

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:07.770
Agent Henderson had a frightening encounter
in the break room.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.979
He was pulling a long shift, and just wanted
to grab some coffee creamer from the cabinet.

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:16.939
However, as he approached the cabinet, he
heard the telltale wheezing, and that terrible,

00:06:16.939 --> 00:06:19.699
overwhelming terror set in once more.

00:06:19.699 --> 00:06:25.930
The Doorman was sitting inside the cabinet
in the fetal position, he just knew it.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:31.000
Could this thing really just appear anywhere
it pleased, and keep people in or out until

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.069
it decided to dematerialize and torment somebody
else?

00:06:34.069 --> 00:06:39.000
When the creature finally dematerialized and
the cabinet was examined, the coffee creamer

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.509
was found to be missing, leaving Agent Henderson
distraught.

00:06:43.509 --> 00:06:48.180
This was the first recorded instance of The
Doorman stealing a physical item, but it would

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.210
be far from the last.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:54.229
Henderson wondered whether the creature that’d
just humiliated him was sitting somewhere

00:06:54.229 --> 00:07:00.469
else now, sipping from a warm cup of joe with
its big, freakish mouth and laughing at him.

00:07:00.469 --> 00:07:06.479
But a few incidents after this, things would
become considerably more serious: The Doorman

00:07:06.479 --> 00:07:08.830
was about to take its first life.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:13.469
Well, it isn’t really that simple, if you
want to get into the semantics of the thing.

00:07:13.469 --> 00:07:18.159
When the body of Dr. Barker was found inside
the 2nd-floor storage room after a spree of

00:07:18.159 --> 00:07:23.550
SCP-303 incidents, the question was naturally
posed as to whether The Doorman had gotten

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:28.080
more dangerous and finally directly attacked
one of its victims.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.080
Not quite.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:33.889
There had only been one way in and out of
the storage room: A secured decompression

00:07:33.889 --> 00:07:39.360
chamber, and the Doorman had appeared inside
this chamber while Dr. Barker was in the storage

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.900
room, effectively trapping him inside with
the sheer terror it causes in its victims.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:49.539
He was trapped in the room for a grand total
of five days, at which point he finally died

00:07:49.539 --> 00:07:54.270
of dehydration, and the Doorman demanifested
shortly afterward.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:59.460
The staff of Site 41 scaled up their countermeasure
efforts, hoping to discover more about and

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:02.830
perhaps even trap and contain the infamous
Doorman.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:09.600
Dr. Burroughs, Researcher Matthews, four members
of security personnel, and four D-Class operatives

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:14.689
formed a kind of strike team, ready for quick
dispatches whenever The Doorman happened to

00:08:14.689 --> 00:08:15.689
manifest.

00:08:15.689 --> 00:08:19.710
It wasn’t long before the creature appeared
in a room on the first floor, but the team

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:24.509
quickly intercepted its location, ready and
eager to gather more data on the mysterious

00:08:24.509 --> 00:08:27.469
being that’d been terrorizing all of them
for weeks.

00:08:27.469 --> 00:08:32.460
Dr. Burroughs ordered one of the D-Classes
to open the door and look inside, but the

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.140
D-Class refused out of fear.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:38.060
The doctor told him that if he didn’t open
the door, he’d be transferred to SCP-682

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.060
duty.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.830
The D-Class frantically shook his head and
said, “I’d rather take my chances with

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.490
the reptile than go in there.”

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.350
The doctor was getting frustrated.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:50.370
He told the D-Class that if he didn’t open
the door immediately, he’d be terminated

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.930
right there on the spot.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:56.570
The D-Class still refused, saying that he’d
take death over what the Doorman would do

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.150
to him if he stepped inside.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:03.170
Without hesitation, Dr. Burroughs ordered
one of the security officers to shoot the

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.570
D-Class then and there.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.140
The shot was fired.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.960
The D-Class was terminated.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:12.440
Dr. Burroughs then ordered a female D-Class
who’d just witnessed this callous execution

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:16.450
to open the door, or the same abrupt death
would befall her.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:20.880
She still refused, then began to describe
the awful things she believed The Doorman

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.750
would do to her if she went inside.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.560
Researcher Matthews was visibly shaken by
the descriptions.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.470
Dr. Burroughs decided not to terminate this
D-Class immediately.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:35.100
He instead wanted to see just how much pressure
the Doorman’s anomalous fear-based resistance

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.180
mechanisms could take.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:41.590
Another D-Class was given a combat knife and
also given the order to cut the female D-Class

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:45.210
with it every time she refused an order to
go inside.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:49.850
After two hours of repeated asking from Dr.
Burroughs, the female D-Class dropped dead

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.020
from blood loss.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:55.010
At no point did she ever attempt to open the
door.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:10:00.230
It seemed that, in all cases for those in
the thrall of the Doorman’s anomalous effects,

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:03.930
death is a truly preferable alternative to
ever facing it head-on.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:09.500
It’s worth mentioning that these tests were
conducted back in the 1970s, before the formation

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:14.600
of the Foundation’s Ethics Committee, which
explains why their methods feel a little needlessly

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:15.600
cruel.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.000
Since then, The Doorman has fully commandeered
the second-floor storage room, the same one

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.460
where it caused Dr. Barker’s death.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:26.250
It only ever leaves the room to steal more
items from around the site.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:30.930
These items have included a cryotube, three
sets of standard Foundation surgical equipment,

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:36.280
two D-Class research cadavers, one gasoline-powered
generator, a variety of chemicals from the

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:41.700
chemical storage areas, and of course, poor
Agent Henderson’s can of powdered coffee

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.700
creamer.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:46.920
The reason for the Doorman taking an interest
in these particular items remains unknown,

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.630
but we can only assume that nothing good can
come of it.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:55.030
And there you have it, folks, the strange,
frightening, and eerily inconclusive tale

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.320
of The Doorman.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:00.820
All we can really say is that we’re awfully
glad he’s fixated on bothering Site 41,

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:04.970
because who knows what would happen if he
widened his net to the rest of us?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.250
Thankfully, we won’t need to think about
that.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.440
Oh, that’s odd.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:09.440
Can you hear that?

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.010
I thought I was imagining it.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.970
Though come to think of it, I can’t help
but feel a little uneasy right now.

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:16.680
Do you ever get that feeling you’re being
watched?

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.670
Wait...The door, there’s something behind
the door.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:20.670
Can you feel it?

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:26.570
Can you feel its red flesh and rotten teeth
pressing up against it, breathing, waiting?

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:29.090
Can you feel it staring at you without eyes?

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:31.060
Looking deep into your very soul?

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.060
No?

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.060
Well, that’s good.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.010
But just stay cautious, okay?

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:41.130
After all, life has many doors, and you never
know who or what will be waiting for you behind

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.340
the next one...

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:49.120
Now go check out “The Deadliest Game - SCP-1918
- Tik Tak Tow” and “SCP-1861 - The Crew

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:53.660
of the HMS Wintersheimer” for more genuinely
frightening anomalies that’ll keep you up

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:54.160
at night!

